### TITLE CARD

### TEA ARIDUCHU

### Why this ending works

The driver never tells whether he confessed. The audience assumes he failed because he stops the story.

Then the phone call quietly reveals he has someone now.

It doesn't explain whether it's the same girl, someone else, or what happened after that college ground. Life moved on. That's the point.

The passenger gets hope without being given an answer. Which is annoyingly human. Nobody ever gets the full script before walking into the airport anyway.
